std::bind (libstdc++ _Bind / _Bind_helper machinery): even the simplest
`std::bind(add, 2, 3)()` fails while instantiating the
`__and_<is_pointer, __not_, is_constructible, ...>` chain of
_Mu/__volget with "member operator got incomplete type on left hand
side", and main's body is dropped.  Dog-food carrier:
src/goto-symex/goto_symex.h:72 constructs shadow_memoryt from
`std::bind(&goto_symext::symex_assign, this, _1, _2, _3)` (a member
function pointer with three placeholders converted to std::function),
whose type stays `nil` so no shadow_memoryt constructor matches.
